/-!
# The inverse capital outer measure and the composite Ville theorem

For a filtration `ℱ` indexed by `ℕ` and a null `S : Set (Measure Ω)`, the inverse capital outer
measure of a set `A ⊆ Ω` is
$$\nu(A)=\inf\{\sup_{P\in S}P(\tau<\infty) :
  \tau\text{ a stopping time},\ A\subseteq\{\tau<\infty\}\}$$
[RLKR23, (2.1)]. Think of `A` as a failure event: `ν A` is the smallest uniform false-alarm
probability of the stopping times that detect `A` in finite time. In terms of sequential tests
(`ProbabilityTheory.IsLevelStoppingTime`), `ν A < α` gives a level-`α` test that rejects whenever
`A` occurs, and conversely a level-`α` test that rejects whenever `A` occurs gives `ν A ≤ α`.
It is an outer measure on all subsets of `Ω` [RLKR23, Lemma 2.1]. It dominates every
member of the null, and for a simple null `{P}` of a finite measure it equals `P` on the
σ-algebra `⨆ n, ℱ n` generated by the filtration.

The composite Ville theorem [RLKR23, Theorem 3.1] says that `ν A = 0` exactly when some
e-process for `S` tends to infinity on `A`. For a simple null `{P}` of a finite measure and an
event `A` of `⨆ n, ℱ n`, it reads as Ville's theorem for e-processes: `P A = 0` exactly when some
e-process for `{P}` tends to infinity on `A`. Its
quantitative form [RLKR23, Theorem 3.7] reads `ν` through e-processes: for every `ε > 0` some
e-process tends to `(ν A + ε)⁻¹` on `A`, and an e-process whose supremum is at least `c` on `A`
gives `ν A ≤ c⁻¹`.

## Main definitions

* `ProbabilityTheory.inverseCapital ℱ S`: the inverse capital outer measure of the null `S` and
  the filtration `ℱ`.

## Main statements

* `ProbabilityTheory.inverseCapital_le_of_isLevelStoppingTime`,
  `ProbabilityTheory.exists_isLevelStoppingTime_of_inverseCapital_lt`,
  `ProbabilityTheory.inverseCapital_eq_zero_iff_forall_exists_isLevelStoppingTime`: the inverse
  capital outer measure through level-`α` sequential tests that are finite on `A`.
* `ProbabilityTheory.measure_le_inverseCapital`: the inverse capital outer measure dominates every
  member of the null.
* `ProbabilityTheory.inverseCapital_eq_iSup_of_measurableSet`: on an event of the filtration it is
  the supremum of the members of the null.
* `ProbabilityTheory.inverseCapital_singleton_apply`: for a simple null `{P}` of a finite measure,
  it equals `P` on the σ-algebra generated by the filtration [RLKR23, Lemma 2.1 (3)].
* `ProbabilityTheory.exists_isEProcess_tendsto_inv_inverseCapital_add`,
  `ProbabilityTheory.IsEProcess.inverseCapital_le_inv`: the two halves of [RLKR23, Theorem 3.7].
* `ProbabilityTheory.inverseCapital_eq_zero_iff`: **the composite Ville theorem**
  [RLKR23, Theorem 3.1].

## Implementation notes

[RLKR23] works with a null of probability measures on `⨆ n, ℱ n`. None of the statements here
assumes that `mΩ = ⨆ n, ℱ n` or that the members of the null are probability measures: Ville's
inequality for e-processes holds at every level for every null
(`ProbabilityTheory.IsEProcess.isLevelStoppingTime_hittingAfter`). Only the simple-null
identity needs a finite measure and a set of `⨆ n, ℱ n`. Its proof covers the set by countably
many events of the filtration of total measure close to its own
(`MeasureTheory.measure_eq_iInf_tsum_of_isSetAlgebra`, Carathéodory's construction), which is the
step [RLKR23] takes from [Bil79, §3].

For `ν A = 0`, the witness e-process is the countable mixture, with weights `2⁻¹ ^ (k + 1)`, of the
one-jump e-processes `α⁻¹ * 𝟙{τ ≤ n}` of level-`α` sequential tests `τ` finite on `A`, at the
levels `α = 4⁻¹ ^ (k + 1)`.

## References

* [Bil79] P. Billingsley, *Probability and Measure*, Wiley Series in Probability and Mathematical
  Statistics, John Wiley & Sons, New York, 1979, §3 (the Carathéodory extension of a probability
  measure from a field of sets).
* [RLKR23] J. Ruf, M. Larsson, W. M. Koolen and A. Ramdas, *A composite generalization of Ville's
  martingale theorem using e-processes*, Electron. J. Probab. 28 (2023), arXiv:2203.04485v3,
  Lemma 2.1, Theorems 3.1 and 3.7.
-/

public section

open MeasureTheory Filter Set
open scoped ENNReal Topology

namespace ProbabilityTheory

variable {Ω : Type*} {mΩ : MeasurableSpace Ω} {ℱ : Filtration ℕ mΩ} {S T : Set (Measure Ω)}
  {P : Measure Ω} {A : Set Ω} {τ : Ω → WithTop ℕ} {α : ℝ≥0∞} {E : ℕ → Ω → ℝ≥0∞}

/-- The value of the inverse capital outer measure, before it is bundled. -/
private noncomputable def inverseCapitalFun (ℱ : Filtration ℕ mΩ) (S : Set (Measure Ω))
    (A : Set Ω) : ℝ≥0∞ :=
  ⨅ (τ : Ω → WithTop ℕ) (_ : IsStoppingTime ℱ τ) (_ : A ⊆ {ω | τ ω < ⊤}),
    ⨆ P ∈ S, P {ω | τ ω < ⊤}

/-- A stopping time finite on `A` bounds the inverse capital outer measure of `A`. -/
private theorem inverseCapitalFun_le (hτ : IsStoppingTime ℱ τ) (hA : A ⊆ {ω | τ ω < ⊤}) :
    inverseCapitalFun ℱ S A ≤ ⨆ P ∈ S, P {ω | τ ω < ⊤} :=
  iInf₂_le_of_le τ hτ (iInf_le _ hA)

/-- Below a value above the inverse capital outer measure of `A`, there is a stopping time finite
on `A`. -/
private theorem exists_of_inverseCapitalFun_lt (h : inverseCapitalFun ℱ S A < α) :
    ∃ τ, IsStoppingTime ℱ τ ∧ A ⊆ {ω | τ ω < ⊤} ∧ ⨆ P ∈ S, P {ω | τ ω < ⊤} < α := by
  obtain ⟨τ, h⟩ := iInf_lt_iff.1 h
  obtain ⟨hτ, h⟩ := iInf_lt_iff.1 h
  obtain ⟨hA, h⟩ := iInf_lt_iff.1 h
  exact ⟨τ, hτ, hA, h⟩

/-- **Countable subadditivity** [RLKR23, Lemma 2.1 (2)]: the infimum of the stopping times that
detect each set detects their union, with a false-alarm probability at most the sum. -/
private theorem inverseCapitalFun_iUnion_le (A : ℕ → Set Ω) :
    inverseCapitalFun ℱ S (⋃ i, A i) ≤ ∑' i, inverseCapitalFun ℱ S (A i) := by
  refine ENNReal.le_of_forall_pos_le_add fun ε hε hlt ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨δ, hδ0, hδ⟩ := ENNReal.exists_pos_sum_of_countable (ENNReal.coe_ne_zero.2 hε.ne') ℕ
  -- a stopping time `τ i` detecting `A i`, within `δ i` of the infimum
  have h_ex : ∀ i, ∃ τ, IsStoppingTime ℱ τ ∧ A i ⊆ {ω | τ ω < ⊤} ∧
      ⨆ P ∈ S, P {ω | τ ω < ⊤} < inverseCapitalFun ℱ S (A i) + δ i := fun i ↦
    exists_of_inverseCapitalFun_lt (ENNReal.lt_add_right
      (ne_top_of_le_ne_top hlt.ne (le_tsum (fun i ↦ inverseCapitalFun ℱ S (A i)) i))
      (ENNReal.coe_ne_zero.2 (hδ0 i).ne'))
  choose τ hτ hAτ hτ_lt using h_ex
  refine (inverseCapitalFun_le (IsStoppingTime.iInf_nat hτ) fun ω hω ↦ ?_).trans (iSup₂_le
    fun P hP ↦ ?_)
  · obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 hω
    have hi' := hAτ i hi
    simp only [mem_ofPred_eq] at hi' ⊢
    exact iInf_lt_iff.2 ⟨i, hi'⟩
  -- the detection event of the infimum is the union of those of the `τ i`
  have h_union : {ω | ⨅ i, τ i ω < ⊤} = ⋃ i, {ω | τ i ω < ⊤} := by
    ext ω
    simp [iInf_lt_iff]
  calc P {ω | ⨅ i, τ i ω < ⊤}
  _ ≤ ∑' i, P {ω | τ i ω < ⊤} := h_union ▸ measure_iUnion_le _
  _ ≤ ∑' i, (inverseCapitalFun ℱ S (A i) + δ i) :=
    tsum_le_tsum fun i ↦ (le_iSup₂_of_le P hP le_rfl).trans (hτ_lt i).le
  _ = ∑' i, inverseCapitalFun ℱ S (A i) + ∑' i, (δ i : ℝ≥0∞) := tsum_add
  _ ≤ ∑' i, inverseCapitalFun ℱ S (A i) + ε := by gcongr

/-- **The inverse capital outer measure** [RLKR23, (2.1)] of a null `S` and a filtration `ℱ`
indexed by `ℕ`: the value at `A ⊆ Ω` is the infimum, over the stopping times `τ` that are finite
on `A`, of the largest probability `⨆ P ∈ S, P {ω | τ ω < ⊤}` that `τ` is finite under a member
of the null (`ProbabilityTheory.inverseCapital_apply`). It is an outer measure on all subsets of
`Ω` [RLKR23, Lemma 2.1]. -/
noncomputable def inverseCapital (ℱ : Filtration ℕ mΩ) (S : Set (Measure Ω)) :
    OuterMeasure Ω where
  measureOf := inverseCapitalFun ℱ S
  empty := by
    -- the stopping time that never stops is finite on `∅`
    refine le_antisymm ((inverseCapitalFun_le (τ := fun _ ↦ ⊤) (fun n ↦ ?_)
      (empty_subset _)).trans (by simp)) bot_le
    simp
  mono hAB := iInf₂_mono fun τ _ ↦ iInf_mono' fun hB ↦ ⟨hAB.trans hB, le_rfl⟩
  iUnion_nat A _ := inverseCapitalFun_iUnion_le A

/-- The value of the inverse capital outer measure at `A`: the infimum, over the stopping times
finite on `A`, of the largest probability under a member of the null that they are finite. -/
theorem inverseCapital_apply (ℱ : Filtration ℕ mΩ) (S : Set (Measure Ω)) (A : Set Ω) :
    inverseCapital ℱ S A = ⨅ (τ : Ω → WithTop ℕ) (_ : IsStoppingTime ℱ τ)
      (_ : A ⊆ {ω | τ ω < ⊤}), ⨆ P ∈ S, P {ω | τ ω < ⊤} := (rfl)

/-! ### Sequential tests that are finite on a set -/

/-- A level-`α` sequential test that is finite on `A` bounds the inverse capital outer measure
of `A` by `α`. -/
theorem inverseCapital_le_of_isLevelStoppingTime (hτ : IsLevelStoppingTime τ ℱ S α)
    (hA : A ⊆ {ω | τ ω < ⊤}) : inverseCapital ℱ S A ≤ α :=
  (inverseCapitalFun_le hτ.isStoppingTime hA).trans (iSup₂_le hτ.measure_lt_top_le)

/-- Above the inverse capital outer measure of `A`, at every level `α`, some level-`α` sequential
test is finite on `A`. -/
theorem exists_isLevelStoppingTime_of_inverseCapital_lt (h : inverseCapital ℱ S A < α) :
    ∃ τ, IsLevelStoppingTime τ ℱ S α ∧ A ⊆ {ω | τ ω < ⊤} := by
  obtain ⟨τ, hτ, hA, hlt⟩ := exists_of_inverseCapitalFun_lt h
  exact ⟨τ, ⟨hτ, fun P hP ↦ (le_iSup₂_of_le P hP le_rfl).trans hlt.le⟩, hA⟩

/-- The inverse capital outer measure of `A` vanishes exactly when, at every level `α ≠ 0`, some
level-`α` sequential test is finite on `A`: the definition [RLKR23, (2.1)] unfolded. -/
theorem inverseCapital_eq_zero_iff_forall_exists_isLevelStoppingTime :
    inverseCapital ℱ S A = 0 ↔
      ∀ α ≠ 0, ∃ τ, IsLevelStoppingTime τ ℱ S α ∧ ∀ ω ∈ A, τ ω < ⊤ := by
  refine ⟨fun h α hα ↦ exists_isLevelStoppingTime_of_inverseCapital_lt
    (h ▸ pos_iff_ne_zero.2 hα), fun h ↦ le_antisymm (ENNReal.le_of_forall_pos_le_add
      fun ε hε _ ↦ ?_) bot_le⟩
  obtain ⟨τ, hτ, hA⟩ := h ε (ENNReal.coe_ne_zero.2 hε.ne')
  simpa using inverseCapital_le_of_isLevelStoppingTime hτ hA

/-! ### The inverse capital outer measure and the members of the null -/

/-- The inverse capital outer measure dominates every member of the null. -/
theorem measure_le_inverseCapital (hP : P ∈ S) (A : Set Ω) : P A ≤ inverseCapital ℱ S A :=
  le_iInf₂ fun _ _ ↦ le_iInf fun hA ↦ (measure_mono hA).trans (le_iSup₂_of_le P hP le_rfl)

/-- The inverse capital outer measure is monotone in the null. -/
theorem inverseCapital_mono (hST : S ⊆ T) : inverseCapital ℱ S ≤ inverseCapital ℱ T :=
  fun _ ↦ iInf₂_mono fun _ _ ↦ iInf_mono fun _ ↦ biSup_mono fun _ hP ↦ hST hP

/-- On an event of the filtration, the inverse capital outer measure is the largest probability
of the event under a member of the null: the stopping time equal to `n` on the event and to `⊤`
off it detects the event at time `n`. -/
theorem inverseCapital_eq_iSup_of_measurableSet {n : ℕ} (hA : MeasurableSet[ℱ n] A) :
    inverseCapital ℱ S A = ⨆ P ∈ S, P A := by
  classical
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (iSup₂_le fun P hP ↦ measure_le_inverseCapital hP A)
  have h_top : IsStoppingTime ℱ fun _ : Ω ↦ (⊤ : WithTop ℕ) := fun k ↦ by simp
  have hτ := (isStoppingTime_const ℱ n).piecewise_of_le h_top (fun _ ↦ le_rfl) (fun _ ↦ le_top) hA
  have h_eq : {ω | A.piecewise (fun _ ↦ WithTop.some n) (fun _ ↦ ⊤) ω < ⊤} = A := by
    ext ω
    by_cases hω : ω ∈ A <;> simp [hω]
  exact (inverseCapitalFun_le hτ h_eq.ge).trans_eq (by rw [h_eq])

/-- **The inverse capital outer measure of a simple null** [RLKR23, Lemma 2.1 (3)]. For a finite
measure `P`, the inverse capital outer measure of `{P}` equals `P` on the σ-algebra `⨆ n, ℱ n`
generated by the filtration. -/
theorem inverseCapital_singleton_apply (P : Measure Ω) [IsFiniteMeasure P]
    (hA : MeasurableSet[⨆ n, ℱ n] A) : inverseCapital ℱ {P} A = P A := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (measure_le_inverseCapital (mem_singleton P) A)
  have hC := isSetAlgebra_iUnion_of_directed_le (fun n ↦ {s | MeasurableSet[ℱ n] s})
    (fun n ↦ @isSetAlgebra_measurableSet _ (ℱ n))
    (Monotone.directed_le fun _ _ h s hs ↦ ℱ.mono h s hs)
  rw [← MeasurableSpace.generateFrom_iUnion_measurableSet] at hA
  -- cover `A` by countably many events of the filtration, of total measure close to `P A`
  rw [measure_eq_iInf_tsum_of_isSetAlgebra P hC (fun s hs ↦ ?_) hA]
  · refine le_iInf fun f ↦ le_iInf fun hf ↦ le_iInf fun hAf ↦ ?_
    calc inverseCapital ℱ {P} A
    _ ≤ inverseCapital ℱ {P} (⋃ i, f i) := measure_mono hAf
    _ ≤ ∑' i, inverseCapital ℱ {P} (f i) := measure_iUnion_le f
    _ = ∑' i, P (f i) := by
      congr 1 with i
      obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 (hf i)
      rw [inverseCapital_eq_iSup_of_measurableSet hn, iSup_singleton]
  · obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := mem_iUnion.1 hs
    exact ℱ.le n s hn

/-! ### The composite Ville theorem -/

/-- **E-processes that tend to the inverse of the inverse capital** [RLKR23, Theorem 3.7 (1)].
For every `ε ≠ 0`, some e-process tends to `(ν A + ε)⁻¹` on `A`: the one-jump process
`(ν A + ε)⁻¹ * 𝟙{τ ≤ n}` of a level-`(ν A + ε)` sequential test `τ` finite on `A`. -/
theorem exists_isEProcess_tendsto_inv_inverseCapital_add (ℱ : Filtration ℕ mΩ)
    (S : Set (Measure Ω)) (A : Set Ω) {ε : ℝ≥0∞} (hε : ε ≠ 0) :
    ∃ E, IsEProcess E ℱ S ∧
      ∀ ω ∈ A, Tendsto (fun n ↦ E n ω) atTop (𝓝 (inverseCapital ℱ S A + ε)⁻¹) := by
  set c := inverseCapital ℱ S A + ε
  -- a level-`c` sequential test finite on `A`: if `c = ∞`, the time `0` will do
  obtain ⟨τ, hτ, hA⟩ : ∃ τ, IsLevelStoppingTime τ ℱ S c ∧ A ⊆ {ω | τ ω < ⊤} := by
    rcases eq_top_or_lt_top (inverseCapital ℱ S A) with h | h
    · refine ⟨fun _ ↦ (0 : ℕ), ⟨isStoppingTime_const ℱ 0, fun _ _ ↦ ?_⟩, fun _ _ ↦ ?_⟩
      · simp [c, h]
      · exact WithTop.coe_lt_top 0
    · exact exists_isLevelStoppingTime_of_inverseCapital_lt (ENNReal.lt_add_right h.ne hε)
  refine ⟨_, hτ.isEProcess_inv_mul_indicator, fun ω hω ↦ tendsto_atTop_of_eventually_const
    (i₀ := (τ ω).untop (hA hω).ne) fun n hn ↦ ?_⟩
  have h_le : τ ω ≤ n := (WithTop.untop_le_iff _).1 hn
  simp [h_le]

/-- **The inverse capital through the supremum of an e-process** [RLKR23, Theorem 3.7 (2)]. If
the supremum over time of an e-process is at least `c` on `A`, then `ν A ≤ c⁻¹`: below every
`c' < c`, the first time the e-process reaches `c'` is a level-`c'⁻¹` sequential test finite
on `A`, by Ville's inequality. -/
theorem IsEProcess.inverseCapital_le_inv (hE : IsEProcess E ℱ S) {c : ℝ≥0∞}
    (hA : ∀ ω ∈ A, c ≤ ⨆ n, E n ω) : inverseCapital ℱ S A ≤ c⁻¹ := by
  refine le_of_forall_gt_imp_ge_of_dense fun d hd ↦ ?_
  -- the threshold `d⁻¹ < c` is exceeded on `A`
  have hdc : d⁻¹ < c := ENNReal.inv_lt_iff_inv_lt.1 hd
  refine inverseCapital_le_of_isLevelStoppingTime (hE.isLevelStoppingTime_hittingAfter d)
    fun ω hω ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := lt_iSup_iff.1 (hdc.trans_le (hA ω hω))
  exact hittingAfter_lt_top_iff.2 ⟨n, Nat.zero_le n, mem_Ici.2 hn.le⟩

/-- **The composite Ville theorem** [RLKR23, Theorem 3.1]. A set `A ⊆ Ω` has inverse capital
outer measure zero exactly when some e-process for the null tends to infinity on `A`. For a
simple null `{P}` of a finite measure and a set of `⨆ n, ℱ n`, this is Ville's theorem, by
`ProbabilityTheory.inverseCapital_singleton_apply`. -/
theorem inverseCapital_eq_zero_iff :
    inverseCapital ℱ S A = 0 ↔
      ∃ E, IsEProcess E ℱ S ∧ ∀ ω ∈ A, Tendsto (fun n ↦ E n ω) atTop (𝓝 ∞) := by
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ?_, fun ⟨E, hE, hA⟩ ↦ le_antisymm ((hE.inverseCapital_le_inv (c := ∞)
    fun ω hω ↦ ?_).trans_eq ENNReal.inv_top) bot_le⟩
  swap
  · exact le_of_tendsto' (hA ω hω) fun n ↦ le_iSup (fun n ↦ E n ω) n
  -- level-`4⁻¹ ^ (k + 1)` sequential tests `τ k` finite on `A`, mixed with weights `2⁻¹ ^ (k + 1)`
  have h_ex : ∀ k : ℕ, ∃ τ, IsLevelStoppingTime τ ℱ S (4⁻¹ ^ (k + 1)) ∧ ∀ ω ∈ A, τ ω < ⊤ :=
    fun k ↦ inverseCapital_eq_zero_iff_forall_exists_isLevelStoppingTime.1 h _
      (pow_ne_zero _ (ENNReal.inv_ne_zero.2 ENNReal.ofNat_ne_top))
  choose τ hτ hA using h_ex
  have hw : ∑' k : ℕ, (2⁻¹ : ℝ≥0∞) ^ (k + 1) = 1 := by
    simp [ENNReal.tsum_geometric_add_one, ENNReal.inv_mul_cancel]
  refine ⟨_, isEProcess_tsum_mul (fun k ↦ (hτ k).isEProcess_inv_mul_indicator) hw.le,
    fun ω hω ↦ ENNReal.tendsto_nhds_top_iff_nat.2 fun N ↦ ?_⟩
  -- from time `τ N ω` on, the term of index `N` alone is `2 ^ (N + 1) > N`
  filter_upwards [eventually_ge_atTop ((τ N ω).untop (hA N ω hω).ne)] with n hn
  have h_le : τ N ω ≤ n := (WithTop.untop_le_iff _).1 hn
  have h_term : (2⁻¹ : ℝ≥0∞) ^ (N + 1) * ((4⁻¹ ^ (N + 1))⁻¹ * {ω | τ N ω ≤ n}.indicator 1 ω) =
      2 ^ (N + 1) := by
    simp [h_le, ← ENNReal.inv_pow, show (4 : ℝ≥0∞) = 2 * 2 by norm_num, mul_pow,
      ENNReal.inv_mul_cancel_left]
  calc (N : ℝ≥0∞) < 2 ^ (N + 1) := by
        exact_mod_cast Nat.lt_two_pow_self.trans (Nat.pow_lt_pow_succ one_lt_two)
  _ = _ := h_term.symm
  _ ≤ ∑' k, 2⁻¹ ^ (k + 1) * ((4⁻¹ ^ (k + 1))⁻¹ * {ω | τ k ω ≤ n}.indicator 1 ω) :=
    le_tsum (fun k ↦ 2⁻¹ ^ (k + 1) * ((4⁻¹ ^ (k + 1))⁻¹ * {ω | τ k ω ≤ n}.indicator 1 ω)) N

end ProbabilityTheory
